The array allocation is a 2D array of 1000 numbers. That's about 8KB of memory. Creating this 60 times per second = creating and GC'ing 480KB/s. Modern JS engines handle this well, but it's still an allocation.

Alternative: Use a flat Float64Array or regular array. A flat array of 1000 elements is one allocation. Or even better — pre-allocate once and reuse.

